menu "System Project Store (stored code)"
    config SYS_PROJECT_PARTITION_LABEL
        string "NVS partition of the stored code"
        default "project"
        help
          Label of the NVS data partition (partitions.csv) holding the stored
          code. Kept apart from the default "nvs" partition so a large program
          doesn't crowd settings, actions or BLE data.

    config SYS_PROJECT_MAX_BYTES
        int "Largest stored code (bytes)"
        default 204800
        range 4096 1048576
        help
          Most bytes one stored frame list may hold. Two generations (the
          committed one and the one being stored) must fit the partition with
          NVS overhead: keep this below about 40 % of the partition size.

    config SYS_PROJECT_CHUNK_SIZE
        int "Chunk size (bytes)"
        default 4000
        range 256 4000
        help
          The frame list is stored as NVS blobs of this size (one RAM buffer
          each for writing and for reading). 4000 fills one NVS page's data area.

    config SYS_PROJECT_LOAD_DELAY_MS
        int "Restart delay after a load command (ms)"
        default 300
        range 50 5000
        help
          The load command restarts the board to replay the stored code; the
          delay lets its response reach the app first.
endmenu
